      "id": 1,
      "text": "Huddinge first appears in records in 1314, making it one of Stockholm region's oldest settlements, once a rural hub of farms and mills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/sweden/stockholm_huddinge"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the farm Huddinge gård, named after a man called Hudde, though scholars still debate the exact origin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/sweden/stockholm_huddinge"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During wartime, Huddinge’s residents would climb nearby hills to light beacons, warning ships of approaching danger across Lake Mälaren.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huddinge_Municipality"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "That beacon‑lighting tradition inspired Huddinge’s coat of arms, a visual nod to its historic warning signals.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huddinge_Municipality"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The municipality surrounds the Flemingsbergsskogen nature reserve, a popular spot where locals stroll through ancient forests.",
